course: dictionary
lesson: 11379
title: Abrupt: sudden, rude or steep
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Abrupt has three main meanings. The first is sudden and unexpected, often in an unpleasant way. «The bus made an abrupt stop, and everyone fell forward.» Nobody expected the stop, and the clues show it was sudden.
explain: The second meaning is short and rude, usually about how someone speaks. «Her answer was abrupt, and she did not even look up.» The clues show the answer was short and not friendly.
explain: The third meaning is about land. An abrupt slope is very steep, like an abrupt cliff. When you meet abrupt, read the words around it and ask: is it a stop, a voice, or a hill?
fact: Abrupt is an adjective, and its adverb is abruptly: «He stopped abruptly at the door.»
fact: «Abrupt» means sudden and unexpected, often in an unpleasant way.
fact: «Abrupt» can also mean short and rude in the way someone speaks, like curt.
fact: «Abrupt» can describe a very steep slope or cliff.
fact: Useful phrases: an abrupt halt, come to an abrupt end, an abrupt manner.
exercise: «The film came to an abrupt end when the power went off.» What does abrupt mean here? | *Sudden and unexpected | Very quiet | Very long and slow
exercise: «Mia's abrupt reply made everyone go quiet.» What does abrupt suggest about how Mia spoke? | Slow and kind | Loud and happy | *Short and rude
exercise: «The path ended at an abrupt drop down the hillside.» What does abrupt mean here? | *Very steep | Very wide | Very warm | Very soft
test: «The lights went out with an abrupt click, and the room was dark.» What does abrupt mean? | *Sudden and unexpected | Gentle | Slow and careful
test: «He stopped abruptly at the door.» Which word in this sentence is the adverb form of abrupt? | stopped | door | *abruptly | at
exam: «The road ended at an abrupt cliff edge.» Which meaning fits best? | Very bright | Sudden and rude | Full of people | *Very steep
